# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, `actions/checkout` on a Windows runner applies `core.autocrlf`
# and hands the build CRLF files. That breaks any test that compares a
# serialised YAML document against the file it was read from, because the
# `yaml` library always emits LF — which is exactly how the v0.2.0 release
# build failed while CI (Linux) stayed green: the release job is the only one
# that runs the suite on windows-latest.
#
# Nothing in this repo needs CRLF. There are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files; the
# Windows side is a WiX .wxs and a WinSW .xml, both of which are XML parsers'
# problems rather than the shell's.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the fixtures that are compared byte-for-byte.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
